\DOC SHARPEN_INEQ_TAC

\TYPE {SHARPEN_INEQ_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Converts a real non-strict inequality goal {t <= u} into the strict inequality
{t < u + &1}.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is a real-valued
inequality {t <= u}, it adds {+ &1} to the right-hand side (parenthesising it
where needed), leaving the assumptions untouched:
{
   A ?- t <= u
   =================  SHARPEN_INEQ_TAC
   A ?- t < u + &1
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces this is the only transformation seen, always on goals
whose conclusion is a {<=} comparison between real terms, with a large
unchanged assumption list.

\ENDDOC
